  "主要内容": "The NASDAQ-100 Index underwent annual re-ranking on Dec 11, 2015, adding seven companies including Ctrip.com International, Ltd. (CTRP), Endo International plc (ENDP), and Expedia, Inc. (EXPE), while removing seven others such as C.H. Robinson Worldwide, Inc. (CHRW) and Wynn Resorts, Limited (WYNN). The re-ranking took effect on Dec 21, 2015, prior to market open. The index includes 100 largest non-financial companies on Nasdaq and is re-ranked annually in December. The NASDAQ-100 Index has returned 3,245% since inception, though past performance does not guarantee future results. The index serves as a benchmark for financial products like options and futures. The PowerShares QQQ Trust (QQQ) tracks the NASDAQ-100 Index performance. Nasdaq is home to over 3,600 listed companies with a market value of approximately $8.8 trillion. Securities explicitly mentioned in the source include Maxim Integrated Products, Inc. (MXIM), Norwegian Cruise Line Holdings Ltd. (NCLH), T-Mobile US, Inc. (TMUS), Ulta Salon, Cosmetics & Fragrance, Inc. (ULTA), Expeditors International of Washington, Inc. (EXPD), Keurig Green Mountain, Inc. (GMCR), Garmin Ltd. (GRMN), Staples, Inc. (SPLS), VimpelCom Ltd. (VIP), LiLAC Class A Ordinary Shares (LILA), LiLAC Class C Ordinary Shares (LILAK), Nasdaq (NDAQ), Index (NDX).",
